<div class="wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3437eebd wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained"><h1 class="wp-block-post-title has-large-font-size has-text-align-center">Internal Bleeding After Abdominal Trauma: Warning Signs You Should Never Ignore</h1>


<div class="wp-block-group is-content-justification-center is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-58cdcb37 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>


<div class="wp-block-post-author-name">Minjin Park</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">·</p>


<div class="wp-block-post-date"><time datetime="2026-07-22T19:03:50+09:00">July 22, 2026</time></div></div>


<figure style="margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)" class="alignwide wp-block-post-featured-image"><img width="941" height="1672" src="https://zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png" class="attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" style="aspect-ratio:4/3;width:100%;object-fit:cover;" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?w=941&amp;ssl=1 941w, https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?resize=169%2C300&amp;ssl=1 169w, https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?resize=576%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 576w, https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?resize=768%2C1365&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?resize=864%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 864w" sizes="(max-width: 941px) 100vw, 941px" data-attachment-id="6813" data-permalink="https://zestyhabit.com/2026/07/22/internal-bleeding-after-abdominal-trauma-warning-signs-you-should-never-ignore/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?fit=941%2C1672&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="941,1672" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-title="f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?fit=576%2C1024&amp;ssl=1" /></figure></div>


<div class="entry-content wp-block-post-content has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-post-content-is-layout-constrained">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img data-recalc-dims="1" decoding="async" width="576" height="1024" data-attachment-id="6813" data-permalink="https://zestyhabit.com/2026/07/22/internal-bleeding-after-abdominal-trauma-warning-signs-you-should-never-ignore/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?fit=941%2C1672&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="941,1672" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-title="f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?fit=576%2C1024&amp;ssl=1" src="https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?resize=576%2C1024&#038;ssl=1" alt="" class="wp-image-6813" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?resize=576%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 576w, https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?resize=169%2C300&amp;ssl=1 169w, https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?resize=768%2C1365&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?resize=864%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 864w, https://i0.wp.com/zestyhabit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/f35c5037-4f8b-455b-bc22-9ac4521a0410.png?w=941&amp;ssl=1 941w" sizes="(max-width: 576px) 100vw, 576px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A hard blow to the abdomen can leave little more than a bruise—or it can damage the intestines, nearby blood vessels, and other organs without producing an obvious external wound. That uncertainty is what makes abdominal trauma particularly dangerous.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Internal bleeding may begin immediately after a car crash, fall, sports collision, assault, or bicycle accident. In other cases, an injured section of bowel or its blood supply deteriorates over several hours before serious symptoms appear. A person may initially feel “mostly fine,” go home, and then develop worsening pain, dizziness, vomiting, or signs of shock.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Visible blood is not required for an intestinal or abdominal injury to be life-threatening. Understanding the warning signs—and knowing when not to wait—can make a critical difference.</p>



<div id="ez-toc-container" class="ez-toc-v2_0_90 counter-hierarchy ez-toc-counter ez-toc-white ez-toc-container-direction">
<div class="ez-toc-title-container">
